WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.146
Welcome to the Federal Modernization
Workbook's developer workbook,

2
00:00:04.146 --> 00:00:05.912
Building Non-Person Identity.

3
00:00:05.912 --> 00:00:09.850
This is Chapter 11: deploying
to test and production.

4
00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:14.175
Each chapter's second lab proves one
piece in a non-production tenant.

5
00:00:14.175 --> 00:00:18.768
This runbook proves them together,
in an order that can be undone:

6
00:00:18.768 --> 00:00:23.275
first in a live test environment,
then, unchanged, in production.

7
00:00:23.275 --> 00:00:27.204
We'll see the safe order,
the settings file, the code,

8
00:00:27.204 --> 00:00:32.187
the evidence, who does what, a dry
run, both stages and the dangers.

9
00:00:32.187 --> 00:00:36.163
One note: nobody has run this
runbook against a live tenant.

10
00:00:36.163 --> 00:00:39.280
The output you'll see comes
from the kit's fixtures.

11
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:44.080
Why a runbook?

12
00:00:44.080 --> 00:00:47.468
Because each second lab
proved one piece on its own.

13
00:00:47.468 --> 00:00:51.930
A deployment proves them together,
against an environment someone depends on.

14
00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:56.691
Stage 1 is a live test: an Entra test
tenant, an Azure test subscription

15
00:00:56.691 --> 00:01:01.118
and an Active Directory test
forest, with production's licenses.

16
00:01:01.118 --> 00:01:05.940
Stage 2 is production, a separate tenant,
so nothing the test stage does can

17
00:01:05.940 --> 00:01:10.605
reach it, and its preflight won't start
unless the test smoke test passed.

18
00:01:10.605 --> 00:01:15.200
The commands are the same both times;
only the settings file changes.

19
00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:22.119
The order follows the
implementation guide's gates and

20
00:01:22.119 --> 00:01:25.425
what Microsoft Learn says each
control can and can't break.

21
00:01:25.425 --> 00:01:28.875
First, inventory and
owners, which only read.

22
00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:33.625
Second, the app management policy, on
a pilot app and the synthetic one.

23
00:01:33.625 --> 00:01:37.461
It has no report-only mode,
but it refuses only a create or

24
00:01:37.461 --> 00:01:41.463
update that breaks it, so an
existing secret keeps working.

25
00:01:41.463 --> 00:01:45.504
Third, a federated credential
and a managed identity beside

26
00:01:45.504 --> 00:01:48.900
the pilot's old secret, for
a thirty-day parallel run.

27
00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:53.113
Fourth, a group managed account,
once the root key has replicated.

28
00:01:53.113 --> 00:01:58.300
Last, Conditional Access for workload
identities, in report-only mode.

29
00:02:02.050 --> 00:02:07.249
One settings file per stage holds every
value the commands need: the tenant,

30
00:02:07.249 --> 00:02:10.687
the cloud, the identities,
the operators, the pilot,

31
00:02:10.687 --> 00:02:14.125
the synthetic objects, the
policies and the rings.

32
00:02:14.125 --> 00:02:17.038
Before any command
runs, the kit checks it.

33
00:02:17.038 --> 00:02:19.705
A secret, or anything that looks like one,

34
00:02:19.705 --> 00:02:23.425
stops the run, and so does a
placeholder nobody replaced.

35
00:02:23.425 --> 00:02:25.675
The pilot's owner can't be an operator.

36
00:02:25.675 --> 00:02:27.945
The file must be for the
stage you're running,

37
00:02:27.945 --> 00:02:31.412
and the smoke-test group managed
account must follow the standard.

38
00:02:31.412 --> 00:02:34.273
Reads sign in as an
app with a certificate,

39
00:02:34.273 --> 00:02:37.650
writes as a person, and
nothing uses a secret.

40
00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:46.012
The runbook's own code is six PowerShell
scripts in the kit's deploy folder.

41
00:02:46.012 --> 00:02:50.412
The preflight runs eleven checks and
snapshots what the rollback restores.

42
00:02:50.412 --> 00:02:53.859
The smoke test runs seven checks
on the synthetic objects,

43
00:02:53.859 --> 00:02:56.875
and its only write is a
probe that should be refused.

44
00:02:56.875 --> 00:02:58.385
The rollback is planned,

45
00:02:58.385 --> 00:03:02.237
then applied only with its approved
hash, and it never deletes.

46
00:03:02.237 --> 00:03:04.539
One script builds the smoke-test group

47
00:03:04.539 --> 00:03:07.200
managed account's plan
for Chapter 6 to apply.

48
00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.800
The last two record
and check the evidence.

49
00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:13.400
Every script has a fixture mode
that sends nothing anywhere,

50
00:03:13.400 --> 00:03:15.270
and there are sixty tests.

51
00:03:19.020 --> 00:03:23.614
The smoke test proves the deployment
end to end on objects nobody depends on,

52
00:03:23.614 --> 00:03:26.895
and you write each expected
result down before it runs.

53
00:03:26.895 --> 00:03:31.495
The synthetic app must appear in the
register with two owners and no secret.

54
00:03:31.495 --> 00:03:34.220
The synthetic service
account must be rated high.

55
00:03:34.220 --> 00:03:37.839
A new secret on the synthetic
app must be refused,

56
00:03:37.839 --> 00:03:40.282
and if it isn't, it's removed at once.

57
00:03:40.282 --> 00:03:43.320
The federated credential
must match exactly.

58
00:03:43.320 --> 00:03:48.345
Each workload policy must be report-only,
with the synthetic assigned directly.

59
00:03:48.345 --> 00:03:52.507
The sign-ins must show the
report-only results, from a beta read.

60
00:03:52.507 --> 00:03:56.730
And the test host must retrieve the
group managed account's password.

61
00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:04.286
Each step ends with a table of
the requirements it supports:

62
00:04:04.286 --> 00:04:10.501
NIST SP 800-53 controls at
the FedRAMP Moderate baseline,

63
00:04:10.501 --> 00:04:15.939
plus OMB M-22-09 and CISA's SCuBA
baselines where they apply, the FedRAMP

64
00:04:15.939 --> 00:04:20.367
twenty X K S I it aligns to, and the
evidence the security officer keeps.

65
00:04:20.367 --> 00:04:23.334
That evidence is produced, not only named:

66
00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:28.306
each script writes a record with the
command, the result, the controls,

67
00:04:28.306 --> 00:04:32.668
the K S I's and every file's hash,
and one script checks every row.

68
00:04:32.668 --> 00:04:38.170
K S I's belong to cloud providers,
and the assessor decides each control.

69
00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:42.845
Who does what?

70
00:04:42.845 --> 00:04:47.288
Every write is a person's, with a role
activated through Privileged Identity

71
00:04:47.288 --> 00:04:51.732
Management for the change window, and
the change record number as the reason.

72
00:04:51.732 --> 00:04:56.958
The identity engineer prepares the stage
and runs the policy and credential steps.

73
00:04:56.958 --> 00:05:01.870
The Conditional Access administrator runs
the workload policies and the rollback.

74
00:05:01.870 --> 00:05:04.802
The server and Active
Directory engineer installs

75
00:05:04.802 --> 00:05:07.870
the group managed account,
which the pipeline creates.

76
00:05:07.870 --> 00:05:10.758
A reader app with a
certificate does the reads.

77
00:05:10.758 --> 00:05:15.397
And each write has an approver: the
change board, the governance officer,

78
00:05:15.397 --> 00:05:19.780
the pilot's owner, a second
reviewer, and the CISO for each ring.

79
00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:27.585
Now the dry run, the chapter's own
commands on the kit's fixtures,

80
00:05:27.585 --> 00:05:31.243
run on November twenty-first
in a scratch copy of the kit.

81
00:05:31.243 --> 00:05:32.681
Nothing leaves the machine.

82
00:05:32.681 --> 00:05:36.242
The test preflight prints
twelve passes and one warning.

83
00:05:36.242 --> 00:05:40.918
The settings file is clean, the
deployment identity uses a certificate,

84
00:05:40.918 --> 00:05:43.612
the Workload ID Premium license is there,

85
00:05:43.612 --> 00:05:47.654
the baseline is recorded, and the
test host and its group exist.

86
00:05:47.654 --> 00:05:51.435
The warning is deliberate: the
fixture's Conditional Access

87
00:05:51.435 --> 00:05:55.593
administrator holds a standing
role, not one eligible through PIM.

88
00:05:55.593 --> 00:05:59.664
Then the group managed account
plan: one outbound-only account,

89
00:05:59.664 --> 00:06:04.240
run by the pipeline, with its
SailPoint request and change record.

90
00:06:07.990 --> 00:06:11.390
The smoke test prints eight
passes: the seven checks,

91
00:06:11.390 --> 00:06:15.027
with the policy check run once
for each workload policy.

92
00:06:15.027 --> 00:06:18.265
The synthetic app has
two owners and no secret.

93
00:06:18.265 --> 00:06:22.202
A new secret is refused, though
that error is the fixture's own,

94
00:06:22.202 --> 00:06:24.565
since Learn doesn't give the real one.

95
00:06:24.565 --> 00:06:27.377
The sign-ins show the report-only results.

96
00:06:27.377 --> 00:06:31.028
And the test host can retrieve the
group managed account's password.

97
00:06:31.028 --> 00:06:35.260
Then the rollback is planned from the
preflight's snapshot: seven actions,

98
00:06:35.260 --> 00:06:39.077
including the synthetic objects'
cleanup, and none of them a delete.

99
00:06:39.077 --> 00:06:43.570
Applied with its hash but without
the apply switch, it's a dry run.

100
00:06:47.320 --> 00:06:51.343
Production's preflight runs against
a fictional production tenant,

101
00:06:51.343 --> 00:06:54.095
with the test stage's
smoke test as its evidence.

102
00:06:54.095 --> 00:06:55.395
Fourteen passes.

103
00:06:55.395 --> 00:07:00.504
The Conditional Access administrator is
now eligible through PIM, and check eleven,

104
00:07:00.504 --> 00:07:05.395
production only, says the test smoke test
passed eight of eight in another tenant.

105
00:07:05.395 --> 00:07:08.488
Then the evidence check on
the test stage says no-go,

106
00:07:08.488 --> 00:07:10.182
and that's right for a dry run.

107
00:07:10.182 --> 00:07:15.222
Steps 1.1 to 1.5 record their
evidence only against a real tenant,

108
00:07:15.222 --> 00:07:20.745
and a dry-run rollback records dry run,
which the go/no-go doesn't accept.

109
00:07:20.745 --> 00:07:23.970
A rollback applied with the
wrong hash sends nothing.

110
00:07:23.970 --> 00:07:26.910
And the deploy tests: sixty pass.

111
00:07:30.710 --> 00:07:32.309
Stage 1 starts by preparing:

112
00:07:32.309 --> 00:07:36.203
the group managed account's retriever
group with the test host in it,

113
00:07:36.203 --> 00:07:40.583
and the synthetic objects, an app with
two owners and a federated credential,

114
00:07:40.583 --> 00:07:44.060
and a service account whose
random password nobody records.

115
00:07:44.060 --> 00:07:46.972
The pilot's policy is created, turned off.

116
00:07:46.972 --> 00:07:52.035
The preflight records the validation
kit's baseline, checks one to ten;

117
00:07:52.035 --> 00:07:57.010
check ten, for AWS GovCloud and O C I,
doesn't apply in this Entra runbook.

118
00:07:57.010 --> 00:07:59.972
And it checks the root key
is more than ten hours old.

119
00:07:59.972 --> 00:08:03.386
Step 1.1 reads every
identity and its owners.

120
00:08:03.386 --> 00:08:06.751
Step 1.2 turns the pilot
policy on for just two apps,

121
00:08:06.751 --> 00:08:09.460
and plans the tenant-wide one for review.

122
00:08:09.460 --> 00:08:12.877
Step 1.3 moves the pilot
to a federated credential

123
00:08:12.877 --> 00:08:16.270
and a managed identity,
beside its old secret.

124
00:08:20.020 --> 00:08:25.033
Step 1.4 puts a group managed account on
a test host, and it isn't made by hand:

125
00:08:25.033 --> 00:08:27.874
it goes through Chapter 6's approved plan,

126
00:08:27.874 --> 00:08:31.383
and the pipeline applies
it with the reviewed hash.

127
00:08:31.383 --> 00:08:36.632
In the test forest only, before the pipeline
exists, a person may send it instead.

128
00:08:36.632 --> 00:08:40.171
On the host, Test A D Service
Account must print true.

129
00:08:40.171 --> 00:08:43.532
Step 1.5 creates the workload policies.

130
00:08:43.532 --> 00:08:48.136
Microsoft Learn says they cover only
single-tenant service principals,

131
00:08:48.136 --> 00:08:51.282
assigned directly, with
block as the only control.

132
00:08:51.282 --> 00:08:54.970
Chapter 8's script creates
every one report-only.

133
00:08:58.720 --> 00:09:01.395
Step 1.6 is the smoke test.

134
00:09:01.395 --> 00:09:05.018
The synthetic app signs in
twice through a GitHub workflow,

135
00:09:05.018 --> 00:09:08.420
once from outside the egress
range and once from inside.

136
00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:11.608
Both succeed, because the
policies are report-only.

137
00:09:11.608 --> 00:09:16.533
After fifteen minutes, so the sign-ins
reach the log, the smoke test runs.

138
00:09:16.533 --> 00:09:22.333
Step 1.7 hashes the evidence folder, which
says no-go until the rollback is done.

139
00:09:22.333 --> 00:09:27.633
Step 1.8 rehearses that rollback,
which disables and never deletes.

140
00:09:27.633 --> 00:09:30.355
Then you deploy again,
and the second smoke test

141
00:09:30.355 --> 00:09:33.720
becomes the evidence
production's preflight needs.

142
00:09:37.470 --> 00:09:40.858
Production starts only when
nine criteria are signed.

143
00:09:40.858 --> 00:09:45.733
The test smoke test passed every check,
after the rollback and re-deployment.

144
00:09:45.733 --> 00:09:47.957
The rollback was rehearsed and filed.

145
00:09:47.957 --> 00:09:50.532
Every hash in the evidence folder matches.

146
00:09:50.532 --> 00:09:53.931
Fourteen days of report-only
sign-ins were reviewed,

147
00:09:53.931 --> 00:09:57.645
with no unexpected failure
from inside the egress range.

148
00:09:57.645 --> 00:10:00.195
The tenant-wide policy plan was approved.

149
00:10:00.195 --> 00:10:04.795
Production's settings, licenses
and PIM eligibility are in place.

150
00:10:04.795 --> 00:10:06.620
The change record is approved.

151
00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.780
And the evidence check passes.

152
00:10:12.530 --> 00:10:16.330
Stage 2 runs the same commands
with the production settings file.

153
00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:21.030
The preflight passes only with the test
smoke test's evidence from another tenant.

154
00:10:21.030 --> 00:10:23.326
Steps 1.1 to 1.5 run unchanged,

155
00:10:23.326 --> 00:10:29.417
then the tenant-wide app management
policy goes on, with its approved hash.

156
00:10:29.417 --> 00:10:34.143
On day thirty-one, the pilot's legacy
account is disabled, never deleted.

157
00:10:34.143 --> 00:10:37.761
Conditional Access is then
enforced one ring at a time,

158
00:10:37.761 --> 00:10:41.781
each after fourteen days of
sign-ins and the CISO's decision.

159
00:10:41.781 --> 00:10:45.418
The smoke test now expects the
outside sign-in to be blocked,

160
00:10:45.418 --> 00:10:47.868
with the message Microsoft Learn gives.

161
00:10:47.868 --> 00:10:50.257
For a week, the drift run checks daily,

162
00:10:50.257 --> 00:10:54.680
and a ring that blocks the wrong
thing goes back to report-only.

163
00:10:58.430 --> 00:10:59.880
Each danger has a guard.

164
00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.621
The kit refuses a secret
in the settings file,

165
00:11:02.621 --> 00:11:04.992
and a test file run against production.

166
00:11:04.992 --> 00:11:10.117
An app management policy has no report-only
mode, so the scope is the safety.

167
00:11:10.117 --> 00:11:13.955
The probe's secret, if it gets
through, is removed at once.

168
00:11:13.955 --> 00:11:17.655
No workload policy is enforced
before its sign-ins are read.

169
00:11:17.655 --> 00:11:21.055
A group managed account waits
ten hours for the root key.

170
00:11:21.055 --> 00:11:23.555
The rollback is rehearsed and recent.

171
00:11:23.555 --> 00:11:29.420
And disabled isn't revoked: tokens already
issued keep working until they expire.

172
00:11:33.170 --> 00:11:34.520
Here's what done looks like.

173
00:11:34.520 --> 00:11:36.374
The change record is approved,

174
00:11:36.374 --> 00:11:40.007
the settings file holds no
secret, and the preflight said go.

175
00:11:40.007 --> 00:11:44.487
In test, the pilot policy covered two
apps, and the old secret and legacy

176
00:11:44.487 --> 00:11:49.121
account were kept through the parallel
run, then disabled, never deleted.

177
00:11:49.121 --> 00:11:52.658
The group managed account came
through Chapter 6's plan,

178
00:11:52.658 --> 00:11:55.657
and every workload policy
started report-only.

179
00:11:55.657 --> 00:11:58.958
The smoke test passed, and
the rollback was rehearsed.

180
00:11:58.958 --> 00:12:02.900
Every criterion was signed,
production rings went one at a time,

181
00:12:02.900 --> 00:12:07.060
the first week's drift was clean,
and every evidence folder checks.
